being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}}, {"canonical_name": "nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 9, "total_mentions": 104, "members": [{"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 12, "variants": ["nature"], "contexts": ["the physical world and its phenomena", "nothing lost or created"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 14, "variants": ["nature"], "contexts": ["subject of natural history", "fundamental force of the universe"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 15, "variants": ["nature", "Nature"], "contexts": ["the natural world and its processes", "natural world and its processes"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 9, "variants": ["Nature", "nature"], "contexts": ["the physical world and its phenomena", "order and variety of the natural world"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["nature", "Nature"], "contexts": ["the phenomena of the physical world", "fundamental character or essence"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 12, "variants": ["Nature"], "contexts": ["great intention of the world", "human constitution and inherent frailty"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 8, "variants": ["Nature", "NATURE", "Natural", "Natures"], "contexts": ["visit my Mother NATURE", "contrasted with Gospel"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 10, "variants": ["Nature", "nature"], "contexts": ["scientific journal", "natural world and its processes"]}, {"entity_id": "nature", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 22, "variants": ["Nature", "nature"], "contexts": ["the physical world and its phenomena", "the physical world"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "nature", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Nature", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Nature", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Nature", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Nature", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Nature", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Nature", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Nature", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2, "stable_key": "clu_b59069eb85cb04f9", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Nature", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "In the context of early modern science and philosophy, 'Nature' often refers to the entirety of the physical world and its phenomena, or the inherent principles governing them.", "wikidata_id": "Q180445", "wikidata_description": "British scientific journal since 1869", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature", "wikipedia_extract": "Nature is an inherent character or constitution, particularly of the ecosphere or the universe as a whole. In this general sense nature refers to the laws, elements and phenomena of the physical world, including life. Although humans are part of nature, human activity or humans as a whole are often described as at times at odds, or outright separate and even superior to nature. During the advent of modern scientific method in the last several centuries, nature became the passive reality, organized and moved by divine laws. With the Industrial Revolution, nature increasingly became seen as the part of reality deprived from intentional intervention: it was hence considered as sacred by some traditions (Rousseau, American transcendentalism) or a mere decorum for divine providence or human history (Hegel, Marx). However, a vitalist vision of nature, closer to the pre-Socratic one, got reborn at the same time, especially after Charles Darwin."}}, {"canonical_name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 8, "total_mentions": 140, "members": [{"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 2, "variants": ["China"], "contexts": ["origin of dishes", "country where porcelain was made"]}, {"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["China"], "contexts": ["region known for monsoon knowledge"]}, {"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 116, "variants": ["China", "Chine", "chinez"], "contexts": ["country of information", "destination for benzoin"]}, {"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["China"], "contexts": ["region of origin for the plant Cina"]}, {"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 4, "variants": ["China"], "contexts": ["country with ancient astronomical records", "country with decimal division of day"]}, {"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 12, "variants": ["China"], "contexts": ["root from the Indies", "country of origin for a root"]}, {"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 3, "variants": ["China"], "contexts": ["origin of Ch\u00e0", "origin of tea"]}, {"entity_id": "china", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "China", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["China"], "contexts": ["country with long-settled political organization"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "China", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "China", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3, "stable_key": "clu_34d0d9eb2be4f69c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "China", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "China", "wikidata_id": "Q148", "wikidata_description": "country in East Asia", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demographics_of_China", "wikipedia_extract": "The People's Republic of China is the second most-populous country in the world with a population exceeding 1.4 billion, only surpassed by India. China was the world's most populous country until being surpassed by India in 2023. In 2025, China's population officially stood at 1.404 billion, which was three million less than the previous year, with the lowest recorded birthrate since at least the proclamation of the People's Republic of China in 1949. China's population has a relatively small youth component, partially a result of the strict enforcement of China's one-child policy that was in effect from 1979 until 2015, which limited urban families to one child and rural families to two. As of 2022, Chinese state media reported the country's total fertility rate to be 1.09, one of the lowest in the world alongside South Korea, Taiwan, Hong Kong and Singapore. Since 2022, deaths have outstripped births in the country.", "description": "Country of origin for various plants, spices, and historical goods."}}, {"canonical_name": "Religion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 8, "total_mentions": 38, "members": [{"entity_id": "religion", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Religion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Religion"], "contexts": ["system of faith and worship"]}, {"entity_id": "religion", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Religion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Religion", "Reli\u2223gion"], "contexts": ["system of faith and worship", "matters of faith and belief"]}, {"entity_id": "religion", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Religion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 28, "variants": ["RELIGION", "Religion", "religion"], "contexts": ["system of faith", "domain of belief and faith"]}, {"entity_id": "religion", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "religion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["religion"], "contexts": ["belief in supernatural power"]}, {"entity_id": "religion", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "religion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["religion"], "contexts": ["religion"]}, {"entity_id": "religion", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "religion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "