and has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass. The composition of sand varies, depending on the local rock sources and conditions, but the most common constituent of sand in inland continental settings and non-tropical coastal settings is silica (silicon dioxide, or SiO2), usually in the form of quartz. Calcium carbonate is the second most common type of sand."}}, {"canonical_name": "nord", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "nord", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "nord", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 6, "variants": ["Nord", "nord"], "contexts": ["northern lands", "northern region"]}, {"entity_id": "north", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "north", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["north"], "contexts": ["arrived from the north"]}, {"entity_id": "north", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "north", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["north"], "contexts": ["direction of travel"]}, {"entity_id": "northern", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "northern", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["northern"], "contexts": ["location of Alpine and Arctic vegetation"]}, {"entity_id": "northern", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "northern", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["northern"], "contexts": ["northern hemisphere, contrasting with south"]}, {"entity_id": "nord", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Nord", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "varia