onic development. Animals form a clade, meaning that they arose from a single common ancestor. Over 1.5 million living animal species have been described, of which around 1.05 million are insects, over 85,000 are molluscs, and around 65,000 are vertebrates. It has been estimated there are as many as 7.77 million animal species on Earth. Animal body lengths range from 8.5 \u03bcm (0.00033 in) to 33.6 m (110 ft).", "description": "Living creatures, sources of bezoars, subject to washing."}}, {"canonical_name": "cancros", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 37, "members": [{"entity_id": "cancers", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Cancers", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 8, "variants": ["Cancers"], "contexts": ["cancers helped by the herb", "disease that spreads and eats"]}, {"entity_id": "c\u00e1ncer", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "c\u00e1ncer", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 1, "variants": ["c\u00e1ncer"], "contexts": ["disease that can be cauterized"]}, {"entity_id": "cancer", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "cancer", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 1, "variants": ["cancer"], "contexts": ["disease that Ceuadilla can kill"]}, {"entity_id": "cancros", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "cancros", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 26, "variants": ["cancros", "Cancro", "Cancros", "cancro"], "contexts": ["cancers", "cancers, chronic and spreading sores"]}, {"entity_id": "cancer", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "cancer", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 1, "variants": ["cancer"], "contexts": ["a morbid growth in the body"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Cancers", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "c\u00e1ncer", "similarity": 