Italy and Monaco to the southeast; Andorra and Spain to the south; and a maritime border with the United Kingdom to the northwest. Its metropolitan area extends from the Rhine to the Atlantic Ocean and from the Mediterranean Sea to the English Channel and the North Sea. Its 18 integral regions\u2014five of which are overseas\u2014span a combined area of 632,702 km2 (244,288 sq mi), with a total population estimated at 69.1 million in 2026. Its capital, largest city and main cultural and economic centre is Paris."}}, {"canonical_name": "Theophrasto", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 29, "members": [{"entity_id": "theophrastus", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Theophrastus", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Theophrastus"], "contexts": ["ancient Greek philosopher and botanist"]}, {"entity_id": "theophrastus", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Theophrastus", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Theophrastus"], "contexts": ["ancient Greek philosopher and botanist"]}, {"entity_id": "theophrastus", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Theophrastus", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Theophrastus"], "contexts": ["ancient Greek philosopher and botanist"]}, {"entity_id": "theophrasto", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Theophrasto", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 20, "variants": ["Theophrasto", "Teofrasto", "Theofrasto", "Theophr.", "Theophrastus"], "contexts": ["ancient Greek philosopher and botanist", "ancient Greek philosopher"]}, {"entity_id": "theophrasto", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Theophrasto", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Theophrasto", "Theophrasteo"], "contexts": ["ancient author on plants", "ancient authority on manna"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Theophrastus", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Theophrastus", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Theophrasto", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Theophrasto", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Theophrastus", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Theophrasto", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Theophrasto", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Theophrasto", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Theophrastus", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Theophrasto", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Theophrasto", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Theophrasto", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 151, "stable_key": "clu_12352750ce9ccd39", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Theophrastus", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": -371, "death_year": -287, "description": "Ancient Greek philosopher and botanist, known for early botanical studies.", "note": "The spelling variation 'Theophrasto' is a common Romance language adaptation.", "wikidata_id": "Q83428", "wikidata_description": "Swiss physician, philosopher, theologian, and alchemist (c. 1493\u20131541)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paracelsus", "wikipedia_extract": "Paracelsus (; German: [pa\u0281a\u02c8ts\u025blz\u028as]; c. 1493 \u2013 24 September 1541), born Theophrastus von Hohenheim (full name Philippus Aureolus Theophrastus Bombastus von Hohenheim), was a Swiss physician, alchemist, lay theologian, and philosopher of the German Renaissance. He was a pioneer in several aspects of the medical revolution of the Renaissance, emphasizing the value of observation in combination with received wisdom. He is credited as the \"father of toxicology\". Paracelsus also had a substantial influence as a prophet or diviner, his \"Prognostications\" being studied by Rosicrucians in the 17th century. Paracelsianism is the early modern medical movement inspired by the study of his works."}}, {"canonical_name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 29, "members": [{"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["country in Central Europe"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["region of various princes", "country where Tragus observed Orpine's use"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["European country"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 10, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["country of Herbart's associationism", "country where phosphorus debate occurred"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 15, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["region Varenius was likely from", "northern region with bright nights in 1831"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Germany", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Germany", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 152, "stable_key": "clu_b8b6e936d75a95ce", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Germany", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "A European country, associated with philosophical movements and scientific debates.", "note": "Includes references to both the country and its nationality.", "wikipedia_extract": "Germany, officially the Federal Republic of Germany, is a country in Western and Central Europe. It lies between the Baltic Sea and the North Sea to the north with the Alps to the south. Its sixteen constituent states have a total population of over 82 million, making it the most populous member state of the European Union. Germany borders Denmark to the north; Poland and the Czech Republic to the east; Austria and Switzerland to the south; and France, Luxembourg, Belgium, and the Netherlands to the west. The nation's capital and most populous city is Berlin and its main financial centre is Frankfurt; the largest urban area is the Ruhr. Settlement in the territory of modern Germany began in the Lower Paleolithic, with various tribes inhabiting it from the Neolithic onward, chiefly the Celts, and Germanic tribes inhabiting the north."}}, {"canonical_name": "Rosewater", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 29, "members": [{"entity_id": "rosewater", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Rosewater", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 9, "variants": ["Rosewater", "Red Rose Water", "Red Rose-water", "Rose Water"], "contexts": ["added to Cawdle", "fragrant liquid made from roses"]}, {"entity_id": "agua_rosada", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "agua rosada", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 1, "variants": ["agua rosada"], "contexts": ["water used to prepare plant remedies"]}, {"entity_id": "agua_rosada", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "agua rosada", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 5, "variants": ["agua rosada"], "contexts": ["preparation mixed with soliman water", "rose water mixed with balsam"]}, {"entity_id": "agua_rosada", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "agua rosada", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 7, "variants": ["agua rosada"], "contexts": ["used for mixing", "scented water"]}, {"entity_id": "agua_rosada", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "agua rosada", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 7, "variants": ["agua rosada", "agua Rosada"], "contexts": ["rose water", "rose water for lotion"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Rosewater", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 0.907}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Rosewater", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 0.907}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Rosewater", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 0.907}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Rosewater", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 0.907}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "agua rosada", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "agua rosada", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "agua rosada", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "agua rosada", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "agua rosada", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "agua rosada", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "agua rosada", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 153, "stable_key": "clu_cfa9640c2de08111", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Rosewater", "confidence": "high", "type": "chemical", "description": "Fragrant liquid distilled from roses, used in medicine and cosmetics.", "wikipedia_extract": "Rose water or rosewater is a flavoured water created by steeping rose petals in water. It is typically made as a by-product during the distillation of rose petals to create rose oil for perfumes. Rose water is widely utilized to flavour culinary dishes and enhance cosmetic products, and it is significant in religious rituals throughout Eurasia. Iran is a major producer, supplying around 90% of the world's rose water demand. Central Iran is home to the annual Golabgiri festival each spring. Thousands of tourists visit the area to celebrate the rose harvest for the production of rosewater."}}, {"canonical_name": "furnace", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 29, "members": [{"entity_id": "furnace", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Furnace", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Furnace"], "contexts": ["heating apparatus", "used in distillation"]}, {"entity_id": "furnace", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "furnace", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["furnace"], "contexts": ["implied heating apparatus"]}, {"entity_id": "furnace", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "furnace", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["furnace"], "contexts": ["implied by distillation"]}, {"entity_id": "fornace", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "fornace", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 8, "variants": ["fornace", "Furnace", "fornace de mattoni", "fornace de vetri", "fornaci"], "contexts": ["used to dry wine lees", "structure where copper is cooked"]}, {"entity_id": "furnace", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "furnace", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 17, "variants": ["Furnace", "furnace"], "contexts": ["a heating apparatus", "instrument for heating"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Furnace", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "furnace", "similarity": 0.99}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Furnace", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "furnace", "similarity": 0.99}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Furnace", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "fornace", "similarity": 0.961}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Furnace", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "furnace", "similarity": 0.99}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "furnace", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "furnace", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "furnace", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "fornace", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "furnace", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "furnace", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "furnace", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "fornace", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "furnace", "target_book": "polyanthe