dy against taking too liberally", "narcotic drug"]}, {"entity_id": "opium", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "opium", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["opium"], "contexts": ["substance that can affect consciousness"]}, {"entity_id": "opium", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "opium", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["opium"], "contexts": ["substance administered as a suppository"]}, {"entity_id": "opium", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "opium", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["opium"], "contexts": ["narcotic drug from poppy"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Opium", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Opium", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Opium", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Opium", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Opium", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Opium", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Opium", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Opium", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "opium", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "opium", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "opium", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "opium", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 242, "stable_key": "clu_b43b3850238a25ac", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "opium", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Papaver somniferum", "family": "Papaveraceae", "description": "Narcotic drug derived from the opium poppy, used medically and recreationally.", "wikipedia_extract": "Papaver somniferum, commonly known as the opium poppy or breadseed poppy, is a species of flowering plant in the family Papaveraceae. It is the species of plant from which both opium and poppy seeds are derived and is also a valuable ornamental plant grown in gardens. Its native range is the western Mediterranean region, but has since been obscured by widespread introduction and cultivation since ancient times to the present day. It is now naturalised across much of the world with temperate climates. Papaver somniferum is an annual herb growing to about 100 centimetres (40 inches) tall. The plant is strongly glaucous, giving a greyish-green appearance, and the stem and leaves bear a sparse distribution of coarse hairs."}}, {"canonical_name": "Spain", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 13, "members": [{"entity_id": "spain", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Spain", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Spain"], "contexts": ["shore location for compass variation", "country in Southwestern Europe"]}, {"entity_id": "spain", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Spain", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Spain"], "contexts": ["native land of Turnsole", "country where the plant grows"]}, {"entity_id": "spain", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Spain", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Spain"], "contexts": ["European country", "country of origin for pointer"]}, {"entity_id": "spain", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "Spain", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Spain"], "contexts": ["origin of alum"]}, {"entity_id": "spain", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Spain", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Spain"], "contexts": ["country with population oscillations", "country with Cortes"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "Spain", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Spain", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 243, "stable_key": "clu_16feb9df060d385d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Spain", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Spain", "wikidata_id": "Q29", "wikidata_description": "country in southwestern Europe with territories in Africa", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spain", "wikipedia_extract": "Spain, officially the Kingdom of Spain, is a country in Southern and Western Europe with territories in North Africa. Featuring the southernmost point of continental Europe, it is the largest country in Southern Europe and the fourth-most populous European Union (EU) member state. Spanning the majority of the Iberian Peninsula, its territory also includes the Canary Islands, in the Eastern Atlantic Ocean; the Balearic Islands, in the Western Mediterranean Sea; and the autonomous cities of Ceuta and Melilla, in mainland Africa. Peninsular Spain is bordered to the north by France, Andorra, and the Bay of Biscay; to the east and south by the Mediterranean Sea and Gibraltar; and to the west by Portugal and the Atlantic Ocean. Spain's capital and largest city is Madrid; other major urban areas include Barcelona, Valencia, Seville, Zaragoza, M\u00e1laga, Murcia, and Palma de Mallorca. In early antiquity, the Iberian Peninsula was inhabited by Celts, Iberians, and other pre-Roman peoples."}}, {"canonical_name": "fornello", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 13, "members": [{"entity_id": "fourneau", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "fourneau", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["fourneau"], "contexts": ["large furnace"]}, {"entity_id": "fourneaux", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "fourneaux", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["fourneaux"], "contexts": ["furnaces"]}, {"entity_id": "fornalhas", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "fornalhas", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["fornalhas"], "contexts": ["used to burn earth for tutia"]}, {"entity_id": "fornello", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "fornello", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 8, "variants": ["fornello", "forne", "fornello a vento", "forno"], "contexts": ["furnace for slow heating", "stove or furnace"]}, {"entity_id": "fornalhas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "fornalhas", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 2, "variants": ["fornalhas", "fornalhas dos Ferreyros"], "contexts": ["furnaces", "blacksmiths' furnaces, used as analogy"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "fourneau", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "fourneaux", "similarity": 0.934}, {"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "fourneau", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "fornello", "similarity": 0.902}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "fourneaux", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "fornalhas", "similarity": 0.888}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "fornalhas", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "fornalhas", "similarity": 0.824}], "id": 244, "stable_key": "clu_9248d23d836fd0be", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "furnaces", "confidence": "high", "type": "object", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "note": "The context suggests a general furnace, with 'smelting furnace' being a specific type mentioned."}}, {"canonical_name": "Angelica", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 13, "members": [{"entity_id": "angelica", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Angelica", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 6, "variants": ["Angelica", "Ange\u2223lica"], "contexts": ["plant with admirable use", "herb with admirable virtues"]}, {"entity_id": "angelica", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "angelica", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "HERB", "count": 1, "variants": ["angelica"], "contexts": ["plant with similar leaves to Coyopatli"]}, {"entity_id": "ang\u00e9lica_archangelica", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Ang\u00e9lica archangelica", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 3, "variants": ["Ang\u00e9lica archangelica"], "contexts": ["plant name", "angelica herb"]}, {"entity_id": "angelica", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "angelica", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "ROOT", "count": 1, "variants": ["angelica"], "contexts": ["fragrant root for pounding"]}, {"entity_id": "angelicas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "angelicas", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["angelicas"], "contexts": ["flower causing uterine accidents", "plant, angelica"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Angelica", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "angelica", "similarity": 0.787}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Angelica", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Ang\u00e9lica archangelica", "similarity": 0.887}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Angelica", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "angelica", "similarity": 0.834}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Angelica", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "angelicas", "similarity": 0.91}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "angelica", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "angelica", "similarity": 0.767}], "id": 245, "stable_key": "clu_c268dd3ed636645c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Angelica", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Angelica archangelica", "family": "Apiaceae", "description": "Aromatic herb with medicinal properties, often used for digestive issues.", "wikipedia_extract": "Angelica archangelica, commonly known as angelica, garden angelica, wild celery, and Norwegian angelica, is a biennial plant from the family Apiaceae, a subspecies of which is cultivated for its sweetly scented edible stems and roots. Like several other species in Apiaceae, its appearance is similar to several poisonous species (Conium, Heracleum, and others), and should not be consumed unless it has been identified with absolute certainty. Synonyms include Archangelica officinalis Hoffm. and Angelica officinalis Moench. During its first year, it grows only leaves, but during its second year, its fluted stem can reach a height of 2.5 meters (just over 8 feet), and the root is used in flavoring preparations. Its leaves consist of numerous small leaflets divided into three principal groups, each of which is again subdivided into three lesser groups. The edges of the leaflets are finely toothed or serrated."}}, {"canonical_name": "Outubro", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 13, "members": [{"entity_id": "october", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "October", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["October"], "contexts": ["month when Misselto berries ripen", "month when berries are ripe"]}, {"entity_id": "octubre", "book_id"