"variants": ["chemical constitution"], "contexts": ["composition of a substance"]}, {"entity_id": "chemical_composition", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "chemical composition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["chemical composition"], "contexts": ["molecules of substances"]}, {"entity_id": "chemical_composition", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "chemical composition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["chemical composition"], "contexts": ["influenced by heat", "produces electricity in galvanic battery"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "composition chimique", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 0.989}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "composition chimique", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "chemical constitution", "similarity": 0.919}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "composition chimique", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 0.989}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "composition chimique", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 0.989}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "chemical constitution", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "chemical constitution", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "chemical constitution", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 273, "stable_key": "clu_cb4cc79db5884490", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Chemical composition", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "Both 'chemical composition' and 'chemical constitution' refer to the same fundamental scientific concept.", "wikidata_id": "Q1263816", "wikidata_description": "concept in chemistry that has different, but similar, meanings if referred to a single pure substance or a mixture", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical%20composition", "wikipedia_extract": "A chemical composition specifies the identity, arrangement, and ratio of the chemical elements making up a compound by way of chemical and atomic bonds. Chemical formulas can be used to describe the relative amounts of elements present in a compound. For example, the chemical formula for water is H2O: this means that each molecule of water is constituted by 2 atoms of hydrogen (H) and 1 atom of oxygen (O). The chemical composition of water may be interpreted as a 2:1 ratio of hydrogen atoms to oxygen atoms. Different types of chemical formulas are used to convey composition information, such as an empirical or molecular formula. Nomenclature can be used to express not only the elements present in a compound but their arrangement within the molecules of the compound."}}, {"canonical_name": "Egypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "egypt", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Egypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Egypt"], "contexts": ["land from which Israelites were led", "ancient land of origin"]}, {"entity_id": "egypt", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Egypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Egypt"], "contexts": ["ancient civilization with early domesticated animals", "geographic location with savages"]}, {"entity_id": "egypt", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Egypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Egypt"], "contexts": ["country with ancient prejudice of being earthquake-free"]}, {"entity_id": "egypt", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Egypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Egypt"], "contexts": ["country with hieroglyphic manuscripts"]}, {"entity_id": "egypt", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Egypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Egypt"], "contexts": ["ancient civilization with rigid social divisions"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "Egypt", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Egypt", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 274, "stable_key": "clu_e565c9eea0cfc369", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Egypt", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "An ancient civilization and geographical location, relevant to medicinal plants and history.", "note": "Includes Portuguese ('Egypto'), French ('Egypte'), and English ('Egypt', 'Egyptian', 'AEgypt').", "wikipedia_extract": "Egypt, officially the Arab Republic of Egypt, is a country spanning the northeast corner of Africa and southwest corner of Asia via the Sinai Peninsula. It is bordered by the Mediterranean Sea to the north, Palestine and Israel to the northeast, the Red Sea to the east, Sudan to the south, and Libya to the west. The Gulf of Aqaba in the northeast separates Egypt from Jordan and Saudi Arabia. Cairo is the capital, largest city, and leading cultural centre, while Alexandria is the second-largest city and an important hub of industry and tourism. With over 107 million inhabitants, Egypt is the third-most populous country in Africa and 15th-most populated in the world. Egypt has one of the longest histories of any country, tracing its heritage along the Nile Delta back to the 6th\u20134th millennia BCE.", "country": "Egypt"}}, {"canonical_name": "Love", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "love", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "love", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["love"], "contexts": ["positive quality, from good principle"]}, {"entity_id": "love", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Love", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Love"], "contexts": ["beyond gifts"]}, {"entity_id": "amor", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "amor", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["amor"], "contexts": ["love"]}, {"entity_id": "love", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Love", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["Love", "love"], "contexts": ["strong affection or desire", "cardinal passion of life"]}, {"entity_id": "amor", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "amor", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["amor"], "contexts": ["emotion that can leave lasting impressions"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "love", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Love", "similarity": 0.978}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "love", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "amor", "similarity": 0.963}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "love", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Love", "similarity": 0.978}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "love", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "amor", "similarity": 0.963}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Love", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "amor", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Love", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Love", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Love", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "amor", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "amor", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Love", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "amor", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "amor", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Love", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "amor", "similarity": 0.947}], "id": 275, "stable_key": "clu_a27f6625f0086e26", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Love", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q204", "wikidata_description": "integer number zero; neutral element for the addition", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/0", "wikipedia_extract": "0 (zero) is a number representing an empty quantity. Adding (or subtracting) 0 to any number leaves that number unchanged; in mathematical terminology, 0 is the additive identity of the integers, rational numbers, real numbers, and complex numbers, as well as other algebraic structures. Multiplying any number by 0 results in 0, and consequently dividing by 0 is generally considered to be undefined in arithmetic. As a numerical digit, 0 plays a crucial role in decimal notation: it indicates that the power of ten corresponding to the place containing a 0 does not contribute to the total. For example, \"205\" in decimal means two hundreds, no tens, and five ones. The same principle applies in place-value notations that uses a base other than ten, such as binary and hexadecimal."}}, {"canonical_name": "cedro", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "cedar", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Cedar", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cedar"], "contexts": ["wood tested for electrical properties"]}, {"entity_id": "cedro", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "cedro", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["cedro"], "contexts": ["cedar wood, contrasted with ahuehuetl"]}, {"entity_id": "cedro", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "cedro", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["cedro"], "contexts": ["precious wood"]}, {"entity_id": "pinus_cedrus", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Pinus cedrus", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Pinus cedrus"], "contexts": ["cedar pine tree"]}, {"entity_id": "cedro", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "cedro", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 5, "variants": ["cedro", "Cedro", "cedri"], "contexts": ["tree mentioned in context of plants", "tree from which Gomma elem I might originate"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Cedar", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "cedro", "similarity": 0.928}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Cedar", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "cedro", "similarity": 0.928}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Cedar", "target_book": "kosm