a_medicinal", "target_name": "veas", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 319, "stable_key": "clu_75be46d3cedebe5c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Veins", "confidence": "high", "type": "anatomy", "description": "Blood vessels that carry blood towards the heart.", "wikipedia_extract": "A vein () is a blood vessel in the circulatory system of humans and most other animals that carries blood towards the heart. Most veins carry deoxygenated blood from the tissues back to the heart; exceptions are those of the pulmonary and fetal circulations which carry oxygenated blood to the heart. In the systemic circulation, arteries carry oxygenated blood away from the heart, and veins return deoxygenated blood to the heart, in the deep veins. There are three sizes of veins: large, medium, and small. Smaller veins are called venules, and the smallest the post-capillary venules are microscopic that make up the veins of the microcirculation. Veins are often closer to the skin than arteries."}}, {"canonical_name": "Cuba", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 242, "members": [{"entity_id": "cuba", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Cuba", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 207, "variants": ["Cuba", "CUBA"], "contexts": ["island of Cuba", "island in the Antilles"]}, {"entity_id": "ile_de_cuba", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Ile de Cuba", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 25, "variants": ["Ile de Cuba", "ILE DE CUBA", "de l'ile de Cuba", "ile de Cuba"], "contexts": ["coastal location", "island whose proximity was announced by odor"]}, {"entity_id": "cuba", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Cuba", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 6, "variants": ["Cuba"], "contexts": ["island near Gulf Stream origin", "island where Coniferae and palms grew"]}, {"entity_id": "cuba", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": 