s (peristalsis) to force the blockage out of the organ, resulting in episodic pain that fluctuates with the contractions. Although the term primarily refers to pain caused by this mechanism, any pain which occurs in episodes or fluctuates in intensity may be termed colic or colicky pain. Colic episodes can cause extreme pain, nausea, sweating, and vomiting. The blockage of important passageways in the body can lead to severe and potentially fatal complications if not cleared, such as cholecystitis in the case of biliary colic, or in kidney stone disease."}}, {"canonical_name": "Quito", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 119, "members": [{"entity_id": "quito", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Quito", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 82, "variants": ["Quito"], "contexts": ["province where Andes peaks are located", "city in Ecuador"]}, {"entity_id": "quito", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Quito", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 28, "variants": ["Quito"], "contexts": ["city in Andes", "equator province for snow-line comparison"]}, {"entity_id": "quito", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Quito", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 8, "variants": ["Quito"], "contexts": ["city from which sulphur vivo was brought", "place with fine sulphur"]}, {"entity_id": "quito", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Quito", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Quito"], "contexts": ["place associated with cinnamon"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Quito", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Quito", "similarity": 0.871}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Quito", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Quito", "similarity": 0.871}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Quito", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Quito", "similarity": 0.871}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Quito", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Quito", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Quito", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Quito", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Quito", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Quito", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 337, "stable_key": "clu_3172f7bd775dd8e3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Quito", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Ecuador", "note": "The contexts confirm this refers to the city of Quito.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name"}}, {"canonical_name": "Seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 119, "members": [{"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 98, "variants": ["Seed", "Seeds", "seed"], "contexts": ["part of the Arsmart plant", "small, black seed of Ladies-Bedstraw"]}, {"entity_id": "seedling", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "seedling", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["seedling"], "contexts": ["young plant"]}, {"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 3, "variants": ["seed"], "contexts": ["part of a plant", "reproductive unit of plants"]}, {"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 15, "variants": ["seed"], "contexts": ["reproductive unit of plants", "unit of reproduction for plants"]}, {"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 2, "variants": ["seed"], "contexts": ["development into a tree", "reproductive unit of a plant"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Seed", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "seedling", "similarity": 0.967}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "seed", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "seed", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "seed", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "seed", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "seed", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "seed", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 338, "stable_key": "clu_fd25c4af762ba6d2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Seed", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "note": "This cluster refers to the botanical seed, a fundamental part of plant reproduction and dispersal, as well as the early stage of a plant's life.", "wikidata_id": "Q40763", "wikidata_description": "embryonic plant enclosed in a protective outer covering (seed coat)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seed", "wikipedia_extract": "In botany, a seed is a plant structure containing an embryo and stored nutrients in a protective coat called a testa. More generally, the term seed means anything that can be sown, which may include seed and husk or tuber. Seeds are the product of the ripened ovule, after the embryo sac is fertilized by sperm from pollen, forming a zygote. The embryo within a seed develops from the zygote and grows within the mother plant to a certain size before growth is halted. The formation of the seed is the defining part of the process of reproduction in seed plants (spermatophytes). Other plants such as ferns, mosses and liverworts, do not have seeds and use water-dependent means to propagate themselves."}}, {"canonical_name": "Serapio", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 118, "members": [{"entity_id": "serapion", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Serapion", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 5, "variants": ["Serapion"], "contexts": ["ancient medical writer", "Serapion the Moor, an Author"]}, {"entity_id": "serapis", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Serapis", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Serapis"], "contexts": ["temple where chariot was suspended"]}, {"entity_id": "serapio", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Serapio", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Serapio", "Seapio"], "contexts": ["medieval medical authority", "attributed mental and heart benefits to Balm"]}, {"entity_id": "serapio", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Serapio", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 105, "variants": ["Serapio", "Sarapio", "Serapiam", "Serapi\u00e3o"], "contexts": ["medical authority", "ancient medical authority"]}, {"entity_id": "serapione", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Serapione", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 5, "variants": ["Serapione"], "contexts": ["Medieval medical authority", "ancient authority on remedies"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Serapion", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Serapio", "similarity": 0.951}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Serapion", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Serapio", "similarity": 0.951}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Serapion", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Serapione", "similarity": 0.992}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Serapis", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Serapio", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Serapis", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Serapio", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Serapis", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Serapione", "similarity": 0.895}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Serapio", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Serapio", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Serapio", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Serapione", "similarity": 0.944}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Serapio", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Serapione", "similarity": 0.944}], "id": 339, "stable_key": "clu_d7648dfb3eaa4b02", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Serapion of Alexandria", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Ancient physician and pharmacologist.", "note": "Refers to Serapion the Younger, a medical writer.", "wikipedia_extract": "Serapion of Alexandria (Ancient Greek: \u03a3\u03b5\u03c1\u03b1\u03c0\u03af\u03c9\u03bd \u1f41 \u1f08\u03bb\u03b5\u03be\u03b1\u03bd\u03b4\u03c1\u03b5\u03cd\u03c2) was a physician who lived in the 3rd century BC. He belonged to the Empiric school, and so much extended and improved the system of Philinus of Cos, that the creation of the school is attributed to him by some ancient writers. Serapion wrote against Hippocrates with much vehemence, but neither this, nor any of his other works, have survived. He is several times mentioned by Celsus, Galen, Caelius Aurelianus, A\u00ebtius, Paulus Aegineta, and Nicolaus Myrepsus. This article incorporates text from a publication now in the public domain: Smith, William, ed. (1870). Dictionary of Greek and Roman Biography and Mythology."}}, {"canonical_name": "fogo", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 117, "members": [{"entity_id": "fire", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "fire", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 14, "variants": ["Fire", "fire"], "contexts": ["mercy of the fire for writings", "drawn out by crab juice"]}, {"entity_id": "fuego", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "fuego", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["fuego"], "contexts": ["elemental quality, contrasted with plant's nature"]}, {"entity_id": "fuoco", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "fuoco", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 13, "variants": ["fuoco"], "contexts": ["used for dissolving and heating substances", "fire used for heating"]}, {"entity_id": "fogo", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "fogo", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 89, "variants": ["fogo", "Fogo", "fogo brandi\u017f\u017fimo", "fogo fortiffimo", "fogo\u017fo"], "contexts": ["elemental fire", "heat source"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "fire", "target_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "target_name": "fuego", "similarity": 0.958}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "fire", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "fuoco", "similarity": 0.948}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "fire", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "fogo", "similarity": 0.969}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "fuego", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "fuoco", "similarity": 0.961}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "fuego", "target_book