"target_name": "Nervios", "similarity": 0.959}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Nervs", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "nervos", "similarity": 0.969}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Nervs", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "nervos", "similarity": 0.969}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Nervios", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "nervos", "similarity": 0.943}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Nervios", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "nervos", "similarity": 0.943}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "nervos", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "nervos", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 341, "stable_key": "clu_a43ca0bde66f6496", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "nerve", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q9620", "wikidata_description": "enclosed, cable-like bundle of axons in the peripheral nervous system", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nerve", "wikipedia_extract": "A nerve is an enclosed, cable-like bundle of nerve fibers (called axons). Nerves have historically been considered the basic units of the peripheral nervous system. A nerve provides a common pathway for the electrochemical nerve impulses called action potentials that are transmitted along each of the axons to peripheral organs or, in the case of sensory nerves, from the periphery back to the central nervous system. Each axon is an extension of an individual neuron, along with other supportive cells such as some Schwann cells that coat the axons in myelin. Each axon is surrounded by a layer of connective tissue called the endoneurium. The axons are bundled together into groups called fascicles, and each fascicle is wrapped in a layer of connective tissue called the perineurium.", "description": "Bundles of fibers transmitting nerve impulses."}}, {"canonical_name": "Cordill\u00e8res", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 112, "members": [{"entity_id": "cordillera", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Cordillera", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 3, "variants": ["Cordillera"], "contexts": ["mountain range", "mountain range in South America"]}, {"entity_id": "cordill\u00e8res", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Cordill\u00e8res", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 107, "variants": ["Cordill\u00e8res", "Cordiljcre", "Cordillera", "Cordill\u00e8re de Andes", "Cordill\u00e8re du littoral", "Cordill\u00e8re occidentale", "Cordill\u00e8res d'Apolobamba", "Cordill\u00e8res de Chachapoyas", "Cordill\u00e8res de Colombia", "Cordill\u00e8res de Huarocheri", "Cordill\u00e8res de Quito", "Cordill\u00e8res de Tarma", "Cordill\u00e8res de Venezuela", "Cordill\u00e8res de Veragua", "Cordill\u00e8res de l'Am\u00e9rique", "Cordill\u00e8res de la Parime", "Cordill\u00e8res du Haut-P\u00e9rou", "Cordill\u00e8res du P\u00e9rou", "Cordill\u00e8res du littoral", "Cordill\u00e8res du littoral de Venezuela"], "contexts": ["mountain range influencing human destiny", "mountain range"]}, {"entity_id": "cordilleres", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Cordilleres", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cordilleres"], "contexts": ["mountain range in the Americas"]}, {"entity_id": "cordilleras", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Cordilleras", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cordilleras"], "contexts": ["mountain range affecting temperature"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Cordillera", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Cordill\u00e8res", "similarity": 0.884}, {"source_book": "origin_of_speci