type of malaria characterized by fevers occurring every fourth day.", "wikipedia_extract": "Quartan fever is one of the four types of malaria which can be contracted by humans. It is specifically caused by the Plasmodium malariae species, one of the six species of the protozoan genus Plasmodium. Quartan fever is a form of malaria where an onset of fever occurs in an interval of three to four days, hence the name \"quartan\". It is transmitted by bites of infected female mosquitoes of the genus Anopheles. Symptoms include fevers which range from approximately 40\u201341 \u00b0C (104\u2013106 \u00b0F) and occur periodically in 72 hour intervals. Although cases of malaria have occurred throughout the world, quartan fever typically occurs in the subtropics."}}, {"canonical_name": "Argento", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 37, "members": [{"entity_id": "argent", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "argent", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["argent"], "contexts": ["precious metal found in mines and rivers", "precious metal"]}, {"entity_id": "argent", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "argent", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 13, "variants": ["argent"], "contexts": ["mines worked at conquest", "precious metal found"]}, {"entity_id": "argento", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Argento", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 17, "variants": ["Argento", "argento", "argento battuto", "argento calcinato", "argento viuo", "argento vivo", "d argento", "l argento"], "contexts": ["silver, a precious metal", "metal from under the earth"]}, {"entity_id": "argent", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "argent", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 5, "variants": ["argent", "argenti vivi", "argentivindea", "argentovivo", "argentum"], "contexts": ["used in medicine", "silver-related substance"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "argent", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "argent", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "argent", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Argento", "similarity": 0.973}, {"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "argent", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "argent", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "argent", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Argento", "similarity": 0.973}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "argent", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "argent", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "Argento", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "argent", "similarity": 0.973}], "id": 408, "stable_key": "clu_77c1f983073fc29a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Silver", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "wikidata_id": "Q1090", "wikidata_description": "allotrope of carbon, mineral, substance", "wikipedia_url": "", "wikipedia_extract": "", "note": "The mention of 'Platinum' alongside 'prata' (Portuguese for silver) is likely an anachronism or a misinterpretation within the text, as platinum was not widely recognized or used in European medicine until much later. Given the overwhelming context of 'prata' and its historical use as silver, this is the most probable referent."}}, {"canonical_name": "Coral", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 37, "members": [{"entity_id": "coral", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "coral", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["coral"], "contexts": ["marine invert