efer to chemical compounds that typically contain carbon, especially those found in living organisms or derived from them."}}, {"canonical_name": "Dorpat", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "dorpat", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "Dorpat", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Dorpat"], "contexts": ["location associated with Schmidt"]}, {"entity_id": "dorpat", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Dorpat", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Dorpat"], "contexts": ["location of Bartels' research"]}, {"entity_id": "dorpat", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Dorpat", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Dorpat"], "contexts": ["location of observation"]}, {"entity_id": "dorpat", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Dorpat", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Dorpat"], "contexts": ["location of astronomical observation", "city where star occultation was observed"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "Dorpat", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Dorpat", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "Dorpat", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Dorpat", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "Dorpat", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Dorpat", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Dorpat", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Dorpat", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Dorpat", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Dorpat", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Dorpat", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Dorpat", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 761, "stable_key": "clu_669cf112fcee3415", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Tartu", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Estonia", "note": "Dorpat is the historical German name for Tartu.", "wikidata_id": "Q13972", "wikidata_description": "second most populous city in Estonia", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tartu", "wikipedia_extract": "Tartu is the second largest city in Estonia after Tallinn. Tartu has a population of 97,759 (as of 2024). It is 186 kilometres (116 miles) southeast of Tallinn and 245 kilometres (152 miles) northeast of Riga, Latvia. Tartu lies on the Emaj\u00f5gi river, which connects the two largest lakes in Estonia, Lake V\u00f5rtsj\u00e4rv and Lake Peipus. From the 13th century until the end of the 19th century, Tartu was known in most of the world by variants of its historical name Dorpat. Tartu, the largest urban centre of southern Estonia, is often considered the \"intellectual capital city\" of the country, especially as it is home to the nation's oldest and most renowned university, the University of Tartu (founded in 1632)."}}, {"canonical_name": "Sulphate of magnesia", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "sulfate_de_magn\u00e9sie", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["sulfate de magn\u00e9sie"], "contexts": ["chemical used to precipitate casein"]}, {"entity_id": "sulfate_de_magn\u00e9sie", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["sulfate de magn\u00e9sie"], "contexts": ["chemical composition of purgative salt"]}, {"entity_id": "sulphate_of_magnesia", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "sulphate of magnesia", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["sulphate of magnesia"], "contexts": ["chemical compound studied"]}, {"entity_id": "sulphate_of_magnesia", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Sulphate of magnesia", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Sulphate of magnesia"], "contexts": ["crystals losing transparency when heated", "chemical salt used in experiments"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "similarity": 0.887}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "sulphate of magnesia", "similarity": 0.986}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Sulphate of magnesia", "similarity": 0.98}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "sulphate of magnesia", "similarity": 0.898}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "sulfate de magn\u00e9sie", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Sulphate of magnesia", "similarity": 0.901}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "sulphate of magnesia", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Sulphate of magnesia", "similarity": 0.997}], "id": 762, "stable_key": "clu_00a236bcea0f4f1a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Magnesium sulfate", "confidence": "high", "type": "chemical", "note": "Also known as Epsom salt, historically used as a purgative.", "wikidata_id": "Q288266", "wikidata_description": "chemical compound", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnesium%20sulfate", "wikipedia_extract": "Magnesium sulfate or magnesium sulphate is a chemical compound, a salt with the formula MgSO4, consisting of magnesium cations Mg2+ (20.19% by mass) and sulfate anions SO2\u22124. It is a white crystalline solid, soluble in water. Magnesium sulfate is usually encountered in the form of a hydrate MgSO4\u00b7nH2O, for various values of n between 1 and 11. The most common is the heptahydrate MgSO4\u00b77H2O, known as Epsom salt, which is a household chemical with many traditional uses, including bath salts. The main use of magnesium sulfate is in agriculture, to correct soils deficient in magnesium (an essential plant nutrient because of the role of magnesium in chlorophyll and photosynthesis). The monohydrate is favored for this use; by the mid 1970s, its production was 2.3 million tons per year with production increasing to approximately 2.6 million tons in 2024."}}, {"canonical_name": "discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "discoveries", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["discoveries"], "contexts": ["act of finding something new or unexpected"]}, {"entity_id": "discoveries", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["discoveries"], "contexts": ["new findings or inventions", "new findings or insights"]}, {"entity_id": "discoveries", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["discoveries"], "contexts": ["results of past and present inquiry"]}, {"entity_id": "scientific_discoveries", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "scientific discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["scientific discoveries"], "contexts": ["new findings in science"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "discoveries", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "discoveries", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "scientific discoveries", "similarity": 0.942}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "discoveries", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "scientific discoveries", "similarity": 0.942}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "scientific discoveries", "similarity": 0.942}], "id": 763, "stable_key": "clu_3eb829e20b8f2cb7", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Discoveries", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q42135811", "wikidata_description": "scientific article published on 18 January 2012"}}, {"canonical_name": "M\u00fcller", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "m\u00fcller", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "M\u00fcller", "category": "PERSON