e": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "This refers to the general concept of an observer, not a specific named individual.", "wikidata_id": "Q830077", "wikidata_description": "being who has a unique consciousness and/or unique personal experiences, or an entity that has a relationship with another entity that exists outside of itself"}}, {"canonical_name": "Praticos", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "praticiens", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "praticiens", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 1, "variants": ["praticiens"], "contexts": ["experienced practitioners' sayings"]}, {"entity_id": "praticiens", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "praticiens", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 1, "variants": ["praticiens"], "contexts": ["practitioners of sugar making"]}, {"entity_id": "praticos", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Praticos", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 10, "variants": ["Praticos", "Practicos"], "contexts": ["experienced medical practitioners", "experienced practitioners"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "praticiens", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "praticiens", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "praticiens", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Praticos", "similarity": 0.868}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "praticiens", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Praticos", "similarity": 0.868}], "id": 1185, "stable_key": "clu_fb44f17ea5c0b9fc", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Doctor", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "A medical practitioner or physician", "wikidata_id": "Q39631", "wikidata_description": "professional who practices medicine", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medical%20doctor", "note": "The term 'Praticos' is a plural noun in Portuguese/Spanish, referring to experienced individuals or practitioners.", "wikipedia_extract": "A medical doctor, also known as a physician (American and Canadian English) or medical practitioner (British English), is a health professional who practices medicine. Medicine aims to promote, maintain or restore health through the study, diagnosis, prognosis and treatment of disease, injury, and other physical and mental conditions. Doctors may focus on certain disease categories, types of patients, and methods of treatment, known as specialities. Others work in general practice, providing continuing and comprehensive medical care to individuals, families. Medical practice requires both thorough knowledge of the medical sciences\u2014such as anatomy, physiology, diseases, and their treatment\u2014and strong competence in applying this knowledge in practice, which forms the art or craft of the profession. Both the role of doctors and the meaning of the word itself vary around the world."}}, {"canonical_name": "Docters", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "docteur", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "docteur", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 2, "variants": ["docteur"], "contexts": ["medical degree holder", "medical practitioner"]}, {"entity_id": "docters", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Docters", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 5, "variants": ["Docters", "Doctor", "Doctors"], "contexts": ["medical practitioners", "medical practitioners who commanded an operation"]}, {"entity_id": "dottori", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Dottori", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 5, "variant