th to 20th centuries with a volcanic explosivity index (VEI) of 4 or higher, and smaller eruptions that resulted in significant damage or fatalities. Note that there may be uncertainties to dates with historical eruptions, and there are likely to be many large eruptions that have not been identified.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_volcanic_eruptions_1500\u20132000"}}, {"canonical_name": "Arm\u00e9nia", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "arm\u00e9nie", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "Arm\u00e9nie", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Arm\u00e9nie"], "contexts": ["region in Western Asia"]}, {"entity_id": "arm\u00e9nia", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Arm\u00e9nia", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 9, "variants": ["Arm\u00e9nia"], "contexts": ["region of origin for substances", "country where benjuy is not found"]}, {"entity_id": "armenia", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Armenia", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Armenia"], "contexts": ["place where borrace is found", "region of origin for a substance"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "Arm\u00e9nie", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Arm\u00e9nia", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "Arm\u00e9nie", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Armenia", "similarity": 0.895}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Arm\u00e9nia", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Armenia", "similarity": 0.897}], "id": 1196, "stable_key": "clu_d5747a3821975819", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Armenia", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "A country in Western Asia and Eastern Europe.", "note": "Refers to the geographical region and country.", "wikipedia_extract": "Armenia, officially the Republic of Armenia, is a landlocked country in the Armenian highlands of West Asia. It is a part of the Caucasus region and is bordered by Turkey to the west, Georgia to the north, Azerbaijan to the east, and Iran and the Azerbaijani exclave of Nakhchivan to the south. Yerevan is the capital, largest city and financial center. The Armenian highlands have been home to the Hayasa-Azzi, Shupria, and Nairi peoples. By at least 600 BC, an archaic form of Proto-Armenian, an Indo-European language, had diffused into the Armenian highlands. The first Armenian state of Urartu was established in 860 BC, and by the 6th century BC it was replaced by the Satrapy of Armenia."}}, {"canonical_name": "Capricorn", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "capricorn", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Capricorn", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 6, "variants": ["Capricorn"], "contexts": ["zodiac sign where Mars is exalted", "zodiac sign"]}, {"entity_id": "capricorne", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Capricorne", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["Capricorne"], "contexts": ["tropic line", "tropical zone"]}, {"entity_id": "capricornio", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Capricornio", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Capricornio"], "contexts": ["zodiac sign"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Capricorn", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Capricorne", "similarity": 0.99}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Capricorn", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Capricornio", "similarity": 0.973}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Capricorne", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Capricornio", "similarity": 0.979}], "id": 1197, "stable_key": "clu_4bf434f66ea043f6", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Tropic of Capricorn", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "The southern-most latitude where the sun can be directly overhead.", "note": "Includes references to the zodiac sign Capricorn and the tropic line.", "wikipedia_extract": "The Tropic of Capricorn (or the Southern Tropic) is the circle of latitude that contains the subsolar point at the December (or southern) solstice. It is thus the southernmost latitude where the Sun can be seen directly overhead. It also reaches 90 degrees below the horizon at solar midnight on the June Solstice. Its northern equivalent is the Tropic of Cancer. The Tropic of Capricorn is one of the five major circles of latitude marked on maps of Earth. Its latitude is currently 23\u00b026\u203209.2\u2033 (or 23.4359\u00b0) south of the Equator, but it is very gradually moving northward, currently at the rate of 0.47 arcseconds, or 15 metres, per year."}}, {"canonical_name": "geological period", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "geological_period", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "geological period", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 7, "variants": ["geological period"], "contexts": ["division of Earth's history", "time in earth's history"]}, {"entity_id": "geological_times", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "geological times", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["geological times"], "contexts": ["periods of earth's history"]}, {"entity_id": "geological_epochs", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "geological epochs", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["geological epochs"], "contexts": ["periods in Earth's history"]}, {"entity_id": "geologic_epochs", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "geologic epochs", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["geologic epochs"], "contexts": ["major divisions of geological time"]}, {"entity_id": "geologic_time", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "geologic time", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["geologic time"], "contexts": ["vast periods of Earth's history"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "geological period", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "geological epochs", "similarity": 0.918}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "geological period", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "geologic epochs", "similarity": 0.92}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "geological period", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "geologic time", "similarity": 0.882}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "geological times", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "geological epochs", "similarity": 0.895}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "geological times", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "geologic epochs", "similarity": 0.894}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "geological times", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "geologic time", "similarity": 0.912}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "geological epochs", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "geologic epochs", "similarity": 0.996}], "id": 1198, "stable_key": "clu_abd