 "TREE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "abeto", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "abeto", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 2, "variants": ["abeto"], "contexts": ["tree with red bark and needle-like leaves", "fir tree"]}, {"entity_id": "abeto", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Abeto", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Abeto"], "contexts": ["tree from which turpentine is collected"]}, {"entity_id": "abeto", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "abeto", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 3, "variants": ["abeto", "abete"], "contexts": ["material for good water vessels", "tree yielding resin"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "abeto", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Abeto", "similarity": 0.804}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "abeto", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "abeto", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Abeto", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "abeto", "similarity": 0.804}], "id": 1630, "stable_key": "clu_d0fced123dca4cab", "ground_truth": {"wikipedia_extract": "Until the end of the Ethiopian monarchy in 1975, there were two categories of nobility in Ethiopia and Eritrea. The Mesafint (Ge'ez: \u1218\u1233\u134d\u1295\u1275 mas\u0101fint, modern transcription mes\u0101fint, singular \u1218\u1235\u134d\u1295 masfin, modern mesfin, \"prince\"), the hereditary royal nobility, formed the upper echelon of the ruling class. The Mekwanint (Ge'ez: \u1218\u12b3\u1295\u1295\u1275 mak\u02b7anint, modern mek\u02b7anint, singular \u1218\u12b0\u1295\u1295 mak\u02b7anin, modern mek\u02b7anin or Amharic: \u1218\u12ae\u1295\u1295 mekonnen, \"officer\") were the appointed nobles, often of humble birth, who formed the bulk of the aristocracy. Until the 20th century, the most powerful people at court were generally members of the Mekwanint appointed by the monarch, while regionally, the Mesafint enjoyed greater influence and power. Emperor Haile Selassie greatly curtailed the power of the Mesafint to the benefit of the Mekwanint, who by then were essentially coterminous with the Ethiopian government. The Mekwanint were officials who had been granted specific offices in the Abyssinian government or court."}}, {"canonical_name": "estoraque", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "estoraque", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "estoraque", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "RESIN", "count": 1, "variants": ["estoraque"], "contexts": ["substance with similar smell to liquidambar"]}, {"entity_id": "estoraque", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "estoraque", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 3, "variants": ["estoraque", "esioraque"], "contexts": ["substance from Ethiopia", "substance similar to lacre"]}, {"entity_id": "estoraque", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "estoraque", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["estoraque"], "contexts": ["aromatic resin used in medicine", "storax, ingredient in pills"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "estoraque", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "estoraque", "similarity": 0.601}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "estoraque", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "estoraque", "similarity": 0.601}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "estoraque", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "estoraque", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1631, "stable_key": "clu_780af9b9b8c44301", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Storax", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "family": "Styracaceae", "note": "Storax is a resin obtained from trees of the genus Styrax. 'Storace calami' likely refers to a specific preparation or source of storax.", "wikidata_id": "Q525062", "wikidata_description": "genus of plants", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Styrax", "wikipedia_extract": "Storace is a surname. Notable people with the surname include: Bernardo Storace (fl.", "description": "Aromatic resin from trees, used in perfumery and medicine."}}, {"canonical_name": "refrigeratoriam", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "refrigerante", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "refrigerante", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["refrigerante"], "contexts": ["cooling property of medicines"]}, {"entity_id": "refrigeration", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "refrigeration", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["refrigeration"], "contexts": ["process of becoming cold"]}, {"entity_id": "refrigeratoriam", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "refrigeratoriam", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["refrigeratoriam", "refrigeratione"], "contexts": ["cooling", "coldness, a quality influencing bodily states"]}, {"entity_id": "refrigerant", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "refrigerant", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 2, "variants": ["refrigerant", "refre\u017fcar"], "contexts": ["to cool, a remedy for tremors", "to cool down, a medicinal action"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "refrigerante", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "refrigeration", "similarity": 0.884}, {"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_16