ians", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Experts in the field of mathematics and geometry.", "wikidata_id": "Q170790", "wikidata_description": "person with an extensive knowledge of mathematics", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematician", "wikipedia_extract": "A mathematician is someone who uses an extensive knowledge of mathematics in their work, typically to solve mathematical problems. Mathematicians are concerned with numbers, data, quantity, structure, space, models, and change. One of the earliest known mathematicians was Thales of Miletus (c. 624 \u2013 c. 546 BC); he has been hailed as the first true mathematician and the first known individual to whom a mathematical discovery has been attributed. He is credited with the first use of deductive reasoning applied to geometry, by deriving four corollaries to Thales's theorem."}}, {"canonical_name": "Torricelli", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "torricelli", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "Torricelli", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Torricelli"], "contexts": ["practiced experimental method", "practiced the experimental method"]}, {"entity_id": "torricelli", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Torricelli", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Torricelli"], "contexts": ["associated with the Torricellian vacuum"]}, {"entity_id": "torricelli", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Torricelli", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Torricelli"], "contexts": ["Italian physicist and mathematician"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "Torricelli", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Torricelli", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "med