r large bodies of saltwater.", "wikidata_id": "Q5083", "wikidata_description": "city in and county seat of King County, State of Washington, United States", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seattle"}}, {"canonical_name": "Ice", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "ice", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Ice", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 11, "variants": ["Ice"], "contexts": ["frozen water, compared to crystal", "compared to crystal formation"]}, {"entity_id": "melted_ice", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "melted ice", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["melted ice"], "contexts": ["frozen water in liquid state"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Ice", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "melted ice", "similarity": 0.935}], "id": 2675, "stable_key": "clu_b0281686c2e7c57c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ice", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q189", "wikidata_description": "Nordic island country in the North Atlantic Ocean", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceland", "wikipedia_extract": "Iceland is a Nordic island country between the Arctic Ocean and the North Atlantic Ocean, located on the Mid-Atlantic Ridge between Europe and North America. It is culturally and politically linked with Europe and is the region's westernmost and most sparsely populated country. Its capital and largest city is Reykjav\u00edk, which is home to about 36% of the country's roughly 390,000 residents (excluding nearby towns/suburbs, which are separate municipalities). The official language of the country is Icelandic. Iceland is on a rift between tectonic plates, and its geologic activity includes geysers and frequent volcanic eruptions. The interior consists of a volcanic plateau with sand and lava fields, mountains and glaciers, and many glacial rivers flow to the sea through the lowlands."}}, {"canonical_name": "Austin", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "austin", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Austin", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 10, "variants": ["Austin"], "contexts": ["referring to Augustine of Hippo", "ancient source cited for heresies"]}, {"entity_id": "st_austin", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "St Austin", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["St Austin"], "contexts": ["language for recognizing existence beyond reach", "ancient authority on knowledge and ignorance"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Austin", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "St Austin", "similarity": 0.87}], "id": 2676, "stable_key": "clu_9b396a36ea0bc732", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Augustine of Hippo", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 354, "death_year": 430, "description": "Early Christian theologian and philosopher, bishop of Hippo Regius.", "wikidata_id": "Q8018", "wikidata_description": "Christian theologian, philosopher, and saint (354\u2013430)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustine%20of%20Hippo", "wikipedia_extract": "Augustine of Hippo ( aw-GUST-in, US also  AW-g\u0259-steen; Latin: Aurelius Augustinus Hipponensis; 13 November 354 \u2013 28 August 430) was a Christian theologian and philosopher from Roman Africa. He was the bishop of Hippo Regius from Thagaste in Numidia Cirtensis, (present-day Souk Ahras, Algeria). His writings deeply influenced the development of Western philosophy and Western Christianity, and he is viewed as one of the most important Church Fathers of the Latin Church in the Patristic Period. His many important works include The City of God, On Christian Doctrine, and Confessions. According to his contemporary, Jerome of Stridon, Augustine \"established anew the ancient Faith\". In his youth he was drawn to the Manichaean faith, and later to the Hellenistic philosophy of Neoplatonism."}}, {"canonical_name": "ass", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "asses", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Asses", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["Asses"], "contexts": ["donkey animals", "animal discussed for gall presence"]}, {"entity_id": "ass", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "ass", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 9, "variants": ["ass"], "contexts": ["domesticated equid species", "animal with transverse bars on legs"]}, {"entity_id": "asses", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Asses", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Asses"], "contexts": ["striped"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Asses", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "ass", "similarity": 0.897}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Asses", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Asses", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2677, "stable_key": "clu_6d0ee48246b30289", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Donkey", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "wikidata_id": "Q19707", "wikidata_description": "subspecies of mammal (donkey as a domesticated subspecies); beast of burden, similar to a horse, but smaller", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey", "wikipedia_extract": "The donkey or ass is a domesticated equine. It derives from the African wild ass, Equus africanus, and may be classified either as a subspecies thereof, Equus africanus asinus, or as a separate species, Equus asinus. It was domesticated in Africa some 5000\u20137000 years ago, and has been used mainly as a working animal since that time. There are more than 40 million donkeys in the world, mostly in underdeveloped countries, where they are used principally as draught or pack animals. While working donkeys are often associated with those living at or below subsistence, small numbers of donkeys or asses are kept for breeding, as pets, and for livestock protection in developed countries. An adult male donkey is a jack or jackass, an adult female is a jenny or jennet, and an immature donkey of either sex is a foal."}}, {"canonical_name": "Wolf", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "wolves", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Wolves", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["Wolves"], "contexts": ["animal causing fear and silence", "animals that attacked people"]}, {"entity_id": "wolf", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Wolf", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Wolf"], "contexts": ["animal associated with vision myths"]}, {"entity_id": "wolf", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Wolf", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 6, "variants": ["wolf", "Wolf"], "contexts": ["predatory mammal", "predatory canine species"]}, {"entity_id": "wolves", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Wolves", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["Wolves", "wolves"], "contexts": ["wild canids", "animals with discussed varieties"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Wolves", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Wolves", "similarity": 0.776}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Wolf", "target_book"