eds' strongly suggests bread, but the context 'cloth for straining' is also present, leading to ambiguity. Given it's a general term, assigning 'food' is the most probable primary meaning in a medical/botanical text.", "wikidata_id": "Q7802", "wikidata_description": "baked food made of flour, water and other ingredients", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bread"}}, {"canonical_name": "esterilidade", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "esterilidad", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "esterilidad", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 2, "variants": ["esterilidad"], "contexts": ["inability to conceive"]}, {"entity_id": "esterilidade", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "esterilidade", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 3, "variants": ["esterilidade"], "contexts": ["inability to conceive", "infertility, inability to conceive"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "esterilidad", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "esterilidade", "similarity": 0.995}], "id": 3677, "stable_key": "clu_fa06224ada41b379", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Sterility", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "Infertility", "note": "The Spanish term 'esterilidad' directly translates to sterility or infertility.", "wikidata_id": "Q179399", "wikidata_description": "inability of a person, animal or plant to reproduce by natural means that is no intervention of contraceptive techniques", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infertility"}}, {"canonical_name": "troncos", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "troncos", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "troncos", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants"