 others or to Fraunhofer's specific work, the identification is uncertain.", "wikidata_id": "Q100483762", "wikidata_description": "street in Magdeburg, Saxony-Anhalt, Germany"}}, {"canonical_name": "governador", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PATRON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "governador", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Governador", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 2, "variants": ["Governador", "gouverneur"], "contexts": ["magistrate title", "official position in missions"]}, {"entity_id": "governador", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "governador", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PATRON", "count": 3, "variants": ["governador", "Governador", "governad\u00f4r"], "contexts": ["ordered bells not to be rung", "ruler seeking to control carnal desires"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Governador", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "governador", "similarity": 0.741}], "id": 3725, "stable_key": "clu_e552dac582ceeaa5", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Governor", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q181888", "wikidata_description": "ruler in Mongol and Turkic cultures, variously describing kings, princes, and governors"}}, {"canonical_name": "transition formation", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "de_transition", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "de transition", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["de transition", "transition"], "contexts": ["transition terrain", "transition rocks"]}, {"entity_id": "transition_formation", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "transition formation", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["transition formation"], "contexts": ["geological period", "geological period/layer"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "de transition", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "transition formation", "similarity": 0.917}], "id": 3726, "stable_key": "clu_c75e5bce532d37ee", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Transition formation", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "This refers to geological strata or periods of transition in rock formation.", "wikipedia_extract": "In chemistry, substance is a unique form of matter with constant chemical composition and characteristic properties. Chemical substances may take the form of a single element or chemical compounds. If two or more chemical substances can be combined without reacting, they may form a chemical mixture. If a mixture is separated to isolate one chemical substance to a desired degree, the resulting substance is said to be chemically pure. Chemical substances can exist in several different physical states or phases (e.g. solids, liquids, gases, or plasma) without changing their chemical composition.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Substance_(chemistry)"}}, {"canonical_name": "Caribbean Islands", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "\u00eeles_caribes", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "\u00eeles Caribes", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["\u00eeles Caribes"], "contexts": ["island group name", "islands"]}, {"entity_id": "caribbean_islands", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Caribbean Islands", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Caribbean Islands"], "contexts": ["islands east of hurricane origin", "islands where hurricanes begin"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "\u00eeles Caribes", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Caribbean Islands", "similarity": 0.934}], "id": 3727, "stable_key": "clu_a94383ca84174dc2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Caribbean", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Multiple", "wikidata_id": "Q664609", "wikidata_description": "region to the center-east of America composed of many islands / coastal regions surrounding the Caribbean Sea"}}, {"canonical_name": "Peloponnesus", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "p\u00e9loponn\u00e8se", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "P\u00e9loponn\u00e8se", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 2, "variants": ["P\u00e9loponn\u00e8se"], "contexts": ["region in Greece", "peninsula in Greece"]}, {"entity_id": "peloponnesus", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Peloponnesus", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 3, "variants": ["Peloponnesus"], "contexts": ["region where Nem\u00e6an Lion fell", "Greek peninsula"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "P\u00e9loponn\u00e8se", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Peloponnesus", "similarity": 0.961}], "id": 3728, "stable_key": "clu_71ceb02427ed1d95", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Peloponnese", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Greece", "wikidata_id": "Q1572648", "wikidata_description": "species of reptile", "wikipedia_extract": "The Peloponnese, Peloponnesus, or Morea, is a peninsula and geographic region in Southern Greece, and the southernmost region of the Balkans. It is connected to the central part of the country by the Isthmus of Corinth land bridge, which separates the Gulf of Corinth from the Saronic Gulf. From the late Middle Ages until the 19th century, the peninsula was known as the Morea, a name still in colloquial use in its demotic form. The peninsula is divided among three administrative regions: most belong to the Peloponnese region, with smaller parts belonging to the West Greece and Attica regions. The Peloponnese is a peninsula located at the southern tip of the mainland, 21,549.6 square kilometres (8,320.3 mi2) in area, and constitutes the southernmost part of mainland Greece. It is connected to the mainland by the Isthmus of Corinth, where the Corinth Canal was constructed in 1893.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peloponnese_wall_lizard"}}, {"canonical_name": "Webb", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "webb", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Webb", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Webb"], "contexts": ["measurer of mountain heights", "measured Himalayan peaks"]}, {"entity_id": "webb", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Webb", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 3, "variants": ["Webb"], "contexts": ["made determination of Dhawalagiri elevation", "provided data on mountain elevations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Webb", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Webb", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3729, "stable_key": "clu_c44a181799cd325d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Thomas Webb", "confidence": "medium", "type": "person", "description": "Mountain height measurer, determined Dhawalagiri elevation.", "note": "Multiple individuals named Webb existed in this period. Context suggests a geographer or surveyor.", "wikidata_id": "Q323549", "wikidata_description": "British astronomer and historian (1807-1885)"}}, {"canonical_name": "Mont-Rose", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "mont-rose", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Mont-Rose", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Mont-Rose"], "contexts": ["mountain name", "mountain"]}, {"entity_id": "mont_rosa", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Mont Rosa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Mont Rosa"], "contexts": ["mountain in the Alps"]}, {"entity_id": "monte_rosa", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Monte Rosa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Monte Rosa"], "contexts": ["mountain in the Alps"]}, {"entity_id": "mount_rosa", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Mount Rosa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Mount Rosa"], "contexts": ["mountain range with icy crevices"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mont-Rose", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Mont Rosa", "similarity": 0.928}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mont-Rose", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Monte Rosa", "similarity": 0.905}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mont-Rose", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Mount Rosa", "similarity": 0.897}], "id": 3730, "stable_key": "clu_f8eaea63cb184e52", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Monte Rosa", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Switzerland, Italy", "wikidata_id": "Q14668", "wikidata_description": "massif in Switzerland and Italy"}}, {"canonical_name": "Popocatepetl", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "popocatepetl", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Popocatepetl", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Popocatepetl"], "contexts": ["volcanoes of Popocatepetl", "volcano in Anahuac group"]}, {"entity_id": "popocatepetl", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Popocatepetl", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Popocatepetl"], "contexts": ["volcano near Tlascala", "volcano in the New World"]}, {"entity_id": "popocatepel", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Popocatepel", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Popocatepel"], "contexts": ["volcanic mountain in Mexico"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Popocatepetl", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Popocatepetl", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Popocatepetl", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Popocatepel", "similarity": 0.953}], "id": 3731, "stable_key": "clu_f3291fd3fd782e20", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Popocat\u00e9petl", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Mexico", "wikidata_id": "Q181157", "wikidata_description": "North America volcano", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popocat%C3%A9petl", "wikipedia_extract": "Popocat\u00e9petl (UK:  POP-\u0259-KAT-\u0259-pet-\u0259l, -\u2060kat-\u0259-PET-\u0259l, US:  POHP-, Spanish: [popoka\u02c8tepetl] ; Nahuatl languages: Pop\u014dcatep\u0113tl [popo\u02d0ka\u02c8tepe\u02d0t\u0361\u026c] ) is an active stratovolcano located in the states of Puebla, Morelos, and Mexico in central Mexico. It lies in the eastern half of the Trans-Mexican Volcanic Belt. At 5,393 m (17,694 ft) it is the second highest peak in Mexico, after Citlalt\u00e9petl (Pico de Orizaba) at 5,636 m (18,491 ft). Popocat\u00e9petl is ranked 89th by prominence. It is linked to the twin volcano of Iztaccihuatl to the north by the high saddle known as the \"Paso de Cort\u00e9s\". Izta-Popo Zoquiapan National Park, wherein the two volcanoes are located, is named after them."}}, {"canonical_name": "gr\u00fcnstein", "category": "SU