862", "target_name": "nervous change", "similarity": 0.986}], "id": 3764, "stable_key": "clu_b0959c38b50ab1d9-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "nervous system activity", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "Encompasses both physiological processes and electrical/chemical changes in nerves."}}, {"canonical_name": "ground", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "ground", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "ground", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["ground"], "contexts": ["basis or foundation", "surface of the earth"]}, {"entity_id": "ground", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "ground", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["ground"], "contexts": ["surface of the earth", "where rain carries electricity"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "ground", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "ground", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3765, "stable_key": "clu_aa4df570361c360f", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ground", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "Ambiguous, could refer to the earth's surface or a metaphorical foundation."}}, {"canonical_name": "confusion", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "confusion", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "confusion", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 2, "variants": ["confusion"], "contexts": ["state of being bewildered or unclear", "uncertainty about object identity"]}, {"entity_id": "confusion_of_perception", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "confusion of perception", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["confusion of perception"], "contexts": ["difficulty in distinguishing sensory input"]}, {"entity_id": "confusion", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "confusion", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["confusion"], "contexts": ["unorganized mental state of an infant"]}, {"entity_id": "confusion_of_thought", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "confusion of thought", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["confusion of thought"], "contexts": ["result from pre-established associations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "confusion", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "confusion", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "confusion", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "confusion of thought", "similarity": 0.948}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "confusion of perception", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "confusion", "similarity": 0.895}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "confusion of perception", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "confusion of thought", "similarity": 0.927}], "id": 3766, "stable_key": "clu_59acb49fed2370bf", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "confusion", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "confusion", "wikidata_id": "Q111529541", "wikidata_description": "2021 Eastercon", "wikipedia_extract": "Sundowning, or sundown syndrome, prevalent among people with some form of dementia, is characterized by increased confusion and restlessness beginning in the late afternoon and early evening. The term sundowning was coined by nurse Lois K. Evans in 1987 due to the association between the person's increased confusion and the setting of the sun. For people with sundown syndrome, a multitude of behavioral problems begin to occur and are associated with long-term adverse outcomes. Sundowning seems to occur more frequently during the middle stages of Alzheimer's disease and mixed dementia and seems to subside with the progression of the person's dementia. People are generally able to understand that this behavioral pattern is abnormal.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sundowning"}}, {"canonical_name": "Schiller", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "schiller", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Schiller", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Schiller"], "contexts": ["poet and playwright", "translator of the \u00c6neid"]}, {"entity_id": "schiller", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Schiller", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 3, "variants": ["Schiller"], "contexts": ["author of poem 'Der Spaziergang'", "author of 'Der Spaziergang'"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Schiller", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Schiller", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3767, "stable_key": "clu_d58f53128470e0b3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Friedrich Schiller", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1759, "death_year": 1805, "description": "German poet, playwright, philosopher, and historian."}}, {"canonical_name": "Fig. 2", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "fig__2", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Fig. 2", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Fig. 2"], "contexts": ["diagram reference"]}, {"entity_id": "fig__6", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Fig. 6", "category": "OBJECT", 