/Metaphysics", "wikipedia_extract": "Metaphysics is the branch of philosophy that examines the basic structure of reality. It is traditionally seen as the study of mind-independent features of the world, but some theorists view it as an inquiry into the conceptual framework of human understanding. Some philosophers, including Aristotle, designate metaphysics as first philosophy to suggest that it is more fundamental than other forms of philosophical inquiry. Metaphysics encompasses a wide range of general and abstract topics. It investigates the nature of existence, the features all entities have in common, and their division into categories of being. An influential division is between particulars and universals."}}, {"canonical_name": "logical", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 3, "members": [{"entity_id": "logic", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "name": "logic", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["logic"], "contexts": ["principles of valid reasoning"]}, {"entity_id": "logical", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "logical", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["logical"], "contexts": ["principle of identity in philosophy", "pertaining to the principles of reasoning"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_1865", "source_name": "logic", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "logical", "similarity": 0.941}], "id": 4326, "stable_key": "clu_6f1f332833c6382c-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Logic", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name"}}, {"canonical_name": "mathematical analysis", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 3, "members": [{"entity_id": "analyse_math\u00e9matique", "book_id": "medecine_experimentale_bernard_186