ina, Chile"}}, {"canonical_name": "Cachemire", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "cachemire", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "Cachemire", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cachemire"], "contexts": ["region near mountains and Siberia"]}, {"entity_id": "cachemire", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Cachemire", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cachemire"], "contexts": ["location with latitude"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "Cachemire", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Cachemire", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 5287, "stable_key": "clu_d6c44b9ce76d9250", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Kashmir", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "India, Pakistan, China", "wikidata_id": "Q720403", "wikidata_description": "city in Razavi Khorasan Province, Iran", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kashmar"}}, {"canonical_name": "rochers de granit", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "rochers_de_granit", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "rochers de granit", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["rochers de granit"], "contexts": ["Igneous rock formations"]}, {"entity_id": "granit_blocks", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "granit blocks", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["granit blocks"], "contexts": ["stone blocks from river cataracts"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "rochers de granit", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "granit blocks", "similarity": 0.947}], "id": 5288, "stable_key": "clu_c6b743ee3d106093-3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Granite", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "wikidata_id": "Q36405", "wikidata_description": "city in Scotland, United Kingdom", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aberdeen", "wikipedia_extract": "Aberdeen (  AB-\u0259r-DEEN;  locally [\u02cce\u02d0b\u0259r\u02c8din]  or [\u02c8e\u02d0b\u0259rdin] ; Scottish Gaelic: Obar Dheathain [\u02c8op\u0259\u027e \u02c8\u029d\u025b.\u026a\u0272]) is a port city in North East Scotland, and is the third most populous Scottish city. Historically, Aberdeen was within the historic county of Aberdeenshire, but is now separate from the council area of Aberdeenshire. Aberdeen City Council is one of Scotland's 32 local authorities (commonly referred to as councils). Aberdeen has a population of 198,590 (2020) for the main urban area and 220,690 (2020) for the wider settlement including outlying localities, making it the United Kingdom's 39th most populous built-up area. Aberdeen has a long, sandy coastline and features an oceanic climate, with cool summers and mild, rainy winters. Aberdeen received royal burgh status from David I of Scotland (1124\u20131153), which transformed the city economically."}}, {"canonical_name": "mini\u00e8res de charbon", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "mini\u00e8res_de_charbon", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "mini\u00e8res de charbon", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["mini\u00e8res de charbon"], "contexts": ["coal mines"]}, {"entity_id": "coal_mines", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Coal mines", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Coal mines"], "contexts": ["excavations for coal"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "mini\u00e8res de charbon", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Coal mines", "similarity": 0.917}], "id": 5289, "stable_key": "clu_69a3e49d5f2dd557-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Mines", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "note": "Refers to excavations for minerals, including coal and gold. 'Minas' in Spanish also refers to mines.", "wikidata_id": "Q820477", "wikidata_description": "place for the extraction of minerals", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mine%20%28mining%29"}}, {"canonical_name": "si\u00e8cles", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "si\u00e8cles", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "si\u00e8cles", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["si\u00e8cles"], "contexts": ["long periods of time"]}, {"entity_id": "si\u00e8cle", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "si\u00e8cle", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["si\u00e8cle"], "contexts": ["period of time"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "si\u00e8cles", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "si\u00e8cle", "similarity": 0.842}], "id": 5290, "stable_key": "clu_317dbd8ab9297edf", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Century", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q155874", "wikidata_description": "genus of plants"}}, {"canonical_name": "fragments", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "fragments", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "fragments", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["fragments"], "contexts": ["fragments"]}, {"entity_id": "segments", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "segments", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["segments"], "contexts": ["distinct parts of a body"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "fragments", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "segments", "similarity": 0.915}], "id": 5291, "stable_key": "clu_a98cd5692d30ef4a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Fragments", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "The context suggests discrete parts or pieces of a larger whole.", "wikidata_id": "Q11086567", "wikidata_description": "portion of an object that is torn, broken off, or dislocated from its original whole"}}, {"canonical_name": "petits cailloux", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "petits_cailloux", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "petits cailloux", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["petits cailloux"], "contexts": ["small pebbles found with ore"]}, {"entity_id": "small_pebbles", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "small pebbles", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["small pebbles"], "contexts": ["inanimate objects at aquarium bottom"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "petits cailloux", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "small pebbles", "similarity": 0.936}], "id": 5292, "stable_key": "clu_1d5896801355db41-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Pebble", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "wikidata_id": "Q29726105", "wikidata_description": "protein-coding gene in the species Drosophila melanogaster"}}, {"canonical_name": "collines", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "collines", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "collines", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["collines"], "contexts": ["hills"]}, {"entity_id": "collinas", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "collinas", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["collinas"], "contexts": ["hills that were buried"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "source_name": "collines", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "collinas", "similarity": 0.984}], "id": 5293, "stable_key": "clu_e0eead2057219cb1", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Hills", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Various", "note": "The term 'hills' and its Spanish equivalent 'collinas' consistently refer to naturally raised areas of land.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hill", "wikipedia_extract": "A hill is a landform that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as mountains. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms. The distinction between a hill and a mountain is unclear and largely subjective, but a hill is universally considered to be not as tall, or as steep as a mountain. Geographers historically regarded mountains as hills greater than 1,000 feet (304.8 meters) above sea level. In contrast, hillwalkers have tended to regard mountains as peaks 2,000 feet (610 m) above sea level."}}, {"canonical_name": "combustibles", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "combustibles", "book_id": "epoques_nature_buffon_1778", "name": "combustibles", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["combustibles"], "contexts": ["materials that can burn"]}, {"entity_id": "combustible_substances", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "combustible substances", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "v