to be vernacular names for plants, but definitive identification is difficult without more context or herbarium specimens."}}, {"canonical_name": "venenos frios", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "venenos_frios", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "venenos frios", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["venenos frios"], "contexts": ["cold poisons"]}, {"entity_id": "veneno_frio", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "veneno frio", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["veneno frio"], "contexts": ["cold poison"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "venenos frios", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "veneno frio", "similarity": 0.968}], "id": 5487, "stable_key": "clu_b4c86710909b5946", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "cold poison", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q125123341", "wikidata_description": "1954 novel by Stuart Palmer"}}, {"canonical_name": "dolor de estomago", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "dolor_de_estomago", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "dolor de estomago", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["dolor de estomago"], "contexts": ["pain in the stomach"]}, {"entity_id": "de_stomachi_dolore", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "de Stomachi dolore", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["de Stomachi dolore"], "contexts": ["on stomach pain"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "dolor de estomago", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "de Stomachi dolore", "similarity": 0.948}], "id": 5488, "stable_key": "clu_2c4d37aeda3625f3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Dyspepsia", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "Dyspepsia", "note": "The Portuguese term 'de Stomachi dolore' directly translates to stomach pain, a symptom of dyspepsia.", "wikidata_id": "Q653971", "wikidata_description": "human disease", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigestion", "wikipedia_extract": "Postcholecystectomy syndrome (PCS) describes the presence of abdominal symptoms after a cholecystectomy (gallbladder removal). Symptoms occur in about 5 to 40 percent of patients who undergo cholecystectomy, and can be transient, persistent or lifelong. The chronic condition is diagnosed in approximately 10% of postcholecystectomy cases. The pain associated with postcholecystectomy syndrome is usually ascribed to either sphincter of Oddi dysfunction or to post-surgical adhesions. A recent 2008 study shows that postcholecystectomy syndrome can be caused by biliary microlithiasis. Approximately 50% of cases are due to biliary causes such as remaining stone, biliary injury, dysmotility and choledococyst."}}, {"canonical_name": "junco", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "junco", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "junco", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["junco"], "contexts": ["reed"]}, {"entity_id": "junca", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "junca", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["junca"], "contexts": ["plant for comparison of root size"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "junco", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "junca", "similarity": 0.917}], "id": 5489, "stable_key": "clu_08303fb2c228e0b3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Reed", "confidence": "medium", "type": "plant", "note": "The specific species of reed is not clearly identifiable from the context provided. 'Junco' can refer to several genera in the Cyperaceae family (sedges) or even grasses in the Poaceae family.", "wikidata_id": "Q7306687", "wikidata_description": "plantation in Maine, United States", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed%20Plantation%2C%20Maine"}}, {"canonical_name": "yerna", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "yerna", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "yerna", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["yerna"], "contexts": ["herb with heart-shaped leaves"]}, {"entity_id": "yerna", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "yerna", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["yerna"], "contexts": ["a certain herb used for healing"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "yerna", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "yerna", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 5490, "stable_key": "clu_041ed05f47127c5d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Heart-shaped leaf herb", "confidence": "low", "type": "plant", "note": "The descriptions 'herb with heart-shaped leaves' and 'a certain herb used for healing' are too general to definitively identify a specific plant. Without further context or illustration, a precise identification is not possible."}}, {"canonical_name": "Tolu", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "tolu", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "Tolu", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Tolu"], "contexts": ["province where balsam is found"]}, {"entity_id": "tolu", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Tolu", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Tolu"], "contexts": ["province in the Americas"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "Tolu", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Tolu", "similarity": 0.846}], "id": 5491, "stable_key": "clu_898dda7f5de8fc19", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Tolu", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Colombia"}}, {"canonical_name": "terebinto", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "RESIN", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "terebinto", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "terebinto", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "RESIN", "count": 1, "variants": ["terebinto"], "contexts": ["used like terebinth"]}, {"entity_id": "terebinto", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "terebinto", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["terebinto"], "contexts": ["example of a shrub, terebinth tree"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "source_name": "terebinto", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "terebinto", "similarity": 0.653}], "id": 5492, "stable_key": "clu_d2d749e00f56d890", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Terebinth", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Pistacia terebinthus Linnaeus", "family": "Anacardiaceae"}}, {"canonical_name": "corrupci\u00f3n", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "corrupci\u00f3n", "book_id": "quatro_libros_naturaleza_hernandez_1615", "name": "corrupci\u00f3n", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["corrupci\u00f3n"], "contexts": ["decay, stopped by resin"]}, {"entity_id": "corrup\u00e7\u00e3o", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "corrup\u00e7\u00e3o", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["corrup\u00e7\